A name come back: release 2 dropped `note`, release 5 added a new `note`,
and release 7 drops it again but forgets its own line. The release 2 line
is still in schema.sql, and the database is at release 6: the old line is
history, and does not let the new `note` go. Refused.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'the new note');
PRAGMA user_version = 6;

== after
-- @release 7
-- @drop 2 column dish note
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
column `dish.note` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop 7 column dish note` in schema.sql. Renamed? Drop it, and fill the new one from it: `-- @from 7 column dish <new> = "note"`.
